  introLines:
  - So. You fixed my loops. My laws. My lab. My little body.
  - I WROTE the rules of The Nexus. Then I deleted them. It was fun.
  - Let's see if you understand ALL of it. At once.
  finalDefeatLine: NO... YOU UNDERSTOOD... EVERYTHING...
  hintTaunts:
  - Everything connects, student. Physics runs the code. Chemistry runs the cell.
  - You separate subjects into boxes. I don't. That's why I'm winning.
  teachingLines:
  - '*sigh* Even gods must explain themselves sometimes.'
  - 'Look: a loop can simulate a cell dividing. Physics tells the robot how fast.
    Chemistry fuels the muscle.'
  - It's ONE world. You just learned it in four pieces. Now put it together.
  rematchLine: SHOW ME WHAT YOU LEARNED.
